      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-advanced-topics-2001-p2.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using \\(\\log \\frac{1}{x}=-\\log x\\) and \\(\\log _{b} a=\\frac{\\log a}{\\log b}\\), we get that the product equals \\(\\frac{(-\\log 2)(-\\log 3) \\cdots(-\\log n)}{\\log n \\cdots \\log 3 \\log 2}=(-1)^{n-1}\\).",
